  "hero-kart-diet-v2": {
   "class": "hero-kart",
   "allowSimplify": true,
   "simplifyRatio": 0.5,
   "simplifyError": 0.01,
   "lockBorder": false,
   "allowJoin": false,
   "keepNamed": true,
   "maxTextureSize": 512,
   "colorTextureQuality": 82,
   "meshoptLevel": "medium",
   "stripUnsampledTextureSlots": true,
   "targetTextureFormat": "jpeg",
   "targetTextureFormatRequiresOpaque": true,
   "notes": "What scripts/diet-kart-bodies.mjs ACTUALLY ships, recorded here because hero-kart-balanced-v1 (ratio 0.08) was never the transform any kart was built with — every kart in src/assets/game/models/karts/ records 'simplify 0.5/0.01' in the runtime manifest. allowJoin is false because Meshy lifts arrive as a single primitive, so join() is a no-op that only risks renaming nodes. stripUnsampledTextureSlots removes normal/metallicRoughness/emissive/occlusion: the runtime kart path is MeshToonMaterial{ gradientMap, map }, which samples base colour ONLY, so every other slot is decoded and uploaded for nothing. targetTextureFormat is pinned so a PNG source cannot survive a resize as a PNG (that is how the 2026-07 fleet shipped 245-350 KB '384x384' normal maps). maxTextureSize is 512 rather than the fleet's 384 because dropping the unsampled maps frees far more than the 384->512 base-colour delta costs. targetTextureFormatRequiresOpaque records that the jpeg pin is CONDITIONAL: JPEG has no alpha channel, so on a MASK/BLEND body the pin would silently fill every cut-out with solid paint while making the file smaller — i.e. every size gate would go greener as the body broke. The script skips the pin for any material whose alphaMode is not OPAQUE and says so on stdout. All nine shipped bodies are OPAQUE, so the exception has never fired; `node scripts/diet-kart-bodies.mjs --verify` fails the build if it ever ships anyway."
  },
